# Call-site ledger of h11 at 1c5b07581f058886c8bdd87adababd7d959dc7ca.
# Decide every `undecided` line; see macro-benchmark/README.md.
#
# The scope rules A, B1-B5 and C are in macro-benchmark/README.md; h11.md
# ("Scope rules") shows how this ledger applies them. Arguments are client
# objects (opaque, B5) or package values that fit the parameter's annotation,
# or that the package's code or tests pass there (B2): a parameter typed
# Type[Sentinel] can receive any sentinel class of the package, a parameter
# typed bytes-like receives no package object. The client never gets a
# ReceiveBuffer (Connection._receive_buffer is private; trailing_data
# returns bytes), and never a reader or writer object.
default reject h11._headers.Headers.__getitem__: no Headers object is subscripted, iterated, unpacked, searched or converted at this site; the operand is a typing construct in an annotation, or a dict, list, tuple, set, str, bytes, bytearray, re.Match, generator or ReceiveBuffer (the Headers sites accept the candidate explicitly)
default reject h11._headers.Headers.__eq__: no operand of this comparison, `in` test, set construction or dict key lookup is a Headers object; the compared values are bytes, bytearrays, ints, strs, lists, tuples, dicts, sets, sentinel classes or event classes, and Headers is unhashable (it defines __eq__ without __hash__), so it is never a dict key or set element

